---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Spousal Support Guides | spousalsupportcalc.com';
const description = 'Plain-English guides on spousal support calculation, state-specific guidelines, dispute strategy, and common misconceptions — reviewed by The Click Lab editorial team.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Spousal Support Guides</h1>
  <p>Plain-language guides written and reviewed by the <a href="/editorial">editorial team</a> with experience in family law and spousal support practice. Each guide covers the legal and practical context behind alimony calculations — what the formulas mean, how state courts exercise discretion, what factors drive outcomes above or below the formula, and what to do when support is contested.</p>

  <h2>Understanding support</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/guides/how-spousal-support-is-calculated">How spousal support is calculated</a> &mdash; Formula and discretion paths, worked examples, duration rules, and the adjustments that change formula outputs in practice.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/state-spousal-support-guidelines">State spousal support guidelines</a> &mdash; State-by-state overview of formula states, discretion-heavy states, duration caps, and how geography affects outcomes for the same fact pattern.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/common-spousal-support-misconceptions">Common spousal support misconceptions</a> &mdash; Eleven widely held misunderstandings about alimony: gender assumptions, tax treatment, permanence, modification, prenups, and the binding force of formulas.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Practical action</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/guides/what-to-do-in-spousal-support-dispute">What to do in a spousal support dispute</a> &mdash; Seven-step guide: consulting counsel, documentation, income disclosure, mediation, tax planning, and trial considerations. Includes what not to do.</li>
  </ul>

  <ul style="margin-top:2rem">
    <li><a href="/methodology">Calculator methodology</a> &mdash; All state-specific formulas, duration guidelines, and adjustment factors documented and sourced.</li>
    <li><a href="/faq">FAQ</a> &mdash; Common questions on who pays, how long, tax treatment, modification, remarriage, and judicial discretion.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Return to the <a href="/">calculator</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
